WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.060
npm projects may pull packages from the
public registry,

2
00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:13.668
private registries, internal mirrors, or
scoped organization registries.

3
00:00:13.748 --> 00:00:20.350
Registry configuration decides where
package names are resolved.

4
00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:28.307
Security teams should understand .npmrc
files, organization-level settings,

5
00:00:28.387 --> 00:00:36.842
CI configuration, and developer
workstation defaults because a package name can mean

6
00:00:36.922 --> 00:00:44.451
different things depending on registry
selection and scope configuration.

7
00:00:44.531 --> 00:00:52.870
Dependency confusion risk appears when an
internal package name can be resolved from

8
00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:59.089
an unintended public source or a
higher-precedence registry.

9
00:00:59.169 --> 00:01:06.234
The defensive lesson is not to experiment
with offensive package names.

10
00:01:06.314 --> 00:01:11.642
The lesson is to configure internal
packages clearly,

11
00:01:11.722 --> 00:01:18.903
use scopes for organization packages, pin
scope-to-registry mappings,

12
00:01:18.983 --> 00:01:21.647
and avoid ambiguous names.

13
00:01:21.727 --> 00:01:29.719
A scoped package such as an organization
namespace gives teams a cleaner boundary

14
00:01:29.799 --> 00:01:34.316
than relying on informal naming
conventions.

15
00:01:34.396 --> 00:01:40.883
Registry control should be part of normal
dependency governance.

16
00:01:40.963 --> 00:01:48.260
Teams can use private registries,
allowlisted sources, package mirrors,

17
00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:55.868
provenance policies, and documented
publishing paths to reduce ambiguity.

18
00:01:55.948 --> 00:02:02.435
Developers should be able to tell where a
package came from and why.

19
00:02:02.515 --> 00:02:09.233
When registry configuration is hidden in a
workstation or pipeline,

20
00:02:09.313 --> 00:02:17.189
dependency behavior becomes harder to
review and easier to misconfigure during

21
00:02:17.269 --> 00:02:23.060
onboarding, incident response, or
environment rebuilds.
